tion.json"} {"question" "q-11007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4x+1}{({x}^{2}+11)}+\\frac{1}{(x-5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5x+3}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{4}{(x-5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{3}{(x-5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+2x+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)$ and get\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+2x+5=(Ax+B)(x-1)+C({x}^{2}+2x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+2(1)+5 & =(A(1)+B)(1-1)+C((1)^{2}+2(1)+3) \\\\ 5+2+5 & =6C \\\\ C & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({0}^{2})+2(0)+5 & =(A(0)+B)(0-1)+C({0}^{2}+2(0)+3) \\\\ 5 & =-B+3C \\\\ 5 & =-B+3(2) \\\\ B & =6-5 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=2$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(2)^{2}+2(2)+5 & =(A(2)+B)(2-1)+C({2}^{2}+2(2)+3) \\\\ 29 & =2A+B+11C \\\\ 29 & =2A+(1)+11(2) \\\\ 2A & =29-23 \\\\ A & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,B=1,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)}=\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73d1f7967d0cc3d206837287dcbcbaa2042b00b226d67b913258704e804e79b0" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}-5x+12}{(2{x}^{2}+3)(x-3)}=\\frac{x+B}{2{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{2}{x-3},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(2{x}^{2}+3)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-5x+12 & =(x+B)(x-3)+2(2{x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)^{2}-5(0)+12 & =(0+B)(0-3)+2(2(0)^{2}+3) \\\\ 12 & =-3B+6 \\\\ 6 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978716/state.json" "file_sha256" "57ce164a08af750120cbd68f267e801bdb796faaf43d21787f7e23c7491a1041" "basis" 836 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-ca